{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Also since yesterday, etc.</b> We learn that all seven days the Holy One, blessed be He, was persuading Moshe at the bush to go on his mission — \"since yesterday,\" \"from the day before,\" \"since You spoke\" — that is three, and three instances of גַּם are augmentations, making six, and he was standing on the seventh day when He said to him, \"This again: send, I pray you, by the hand of him whom You will send,\" until He grew angry with him and he accepted it upon himself (Shemot Rabbah). And all this was because he did not wish to assume greatness over Aharon his brother, who was older than him and was a prophet, as it says, \"Did I reveal Myself to your father's house when they were in Egypt?\" (1 Samuel 2) — that is Aharon; and likewise, \"I made Myself known to them in the land of Egypt… and I said to them: Let each man cast away the abominations of his eyes\" (Ezekiel 20) — and that prophecy was spoken to Aharon (Tanchuma)." "<b>Heavy of mouth.</b> I speak with difficulty. And in la'az: בלב\"ו."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "the la'az בלב\"ו is Old French belevoi or equivalent, 'I am heavy/sluggish' (cf. modern French bégayer-related forms); the exact Old French form is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:30.595045090Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}